# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials for `npm run fetch`. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
# The site works with NONE of these set — every figure on both pages already
# comes from a live, keyless, CORS-open endpoint. These only raise limits and
# fidelity. Nothing here is ever bundled into the pages; the fetch script runs
# on your machine (or in CI) and writes plain data to data/snapshot.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GitHub personal access token — https://github.com/settings/tokens
#
#   Fine-grained token, no account permissions needed. "Public repositories
#   (read-only)" is enough; a classic token needs no scopes at all for public
#   data. Add `read:user` if you want the contributions calendar from GitHub
#   itself rather than the public mirror.
#
# What it buys you:
#   - REST limit 60/hr -> 5,000/hr (matters if you rebuild often)
#   - The real contributions calendar via the GraphQL API, instead of the
#     keyless mirror at github-contributions-api.jogruber.de
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Codeforces API key pair — https://codeforces.com/settings/api
#
#   Recommended. Signed requests make user.status include your private-group
#   submissions with exact times: every solve gets its real date, and private
#   solves not yet synced to the solutions repository are counted and listed.
#   Also add both as repository secrets (Settings -> Secrets and variables ->
#   Actions) so the hourly workflow can do the same.
CF_API_KEY=
CF_API_SECRET=
